## The Leaderboard Refuses to Budge

If you were hoping for major movement in the FEBU Pick'em standings this week, you probably left disappointed.

This past slate of games handed out plenty of losses across the board, and nobody really managed to separate themselves from the pack. Between unexpected results, missed picks, and generally questionable decision-making from all involved, the standings remained surprisingly tight.

The biggest winner of the week?

Talesofderp.

While everyone else was busy missing games, Talesofderp managed to come closest to the score prediction and picked up the all-important bonus point.

In a season where every point matters, those bonus points are starting to feel more valuable every week.

### Sco Still Sitting on Top

Despite the chaos, one thing remains unchanged.

Sco is still leading the pack.

The lead isn't exactly comfortable, but it's enough to keep everyone else looking up at the standings for another week.

With several weeks still to play, there's plenty of football left, but opportunities to make up ground are quickly disappearing.

One huge week can still change everything.

One terrible week can send championship dreams into a ditch.

The pressure is starting to build.

### Oregon Walks Into The Shoe and Walks Out With a Win

As for the Ducks?

What a night.

Oregon went into The Shoe and left with a statement victory, taking down Ohio State in one of the toughest environments in college football.

Winning at home is nice.

Winning on the road is better.

Winning in Columbus is the kind of result that gets everyone's attention.

The Ducks looked poised, confident, and completely unfazed by the atmosphere.

It's the kind of win that reminds the rest of the country that Oregon isn't just a playoff contender. They're one of the teams everyone else has to worry about.

### Next Up: Michigan

Now the attention turns to Michigan.

The Wolverines come to Autzen, and while the matchup is intriguing on its own, there's one question everyone seems to be asking:

Who starts at quarterback?

Do the Wolverines roll with Bryce Underwood, the highly touted young quarterback that fans have been waiting to see?

Or do they give the nod to Jadyn Carr and let the veteran experience lead the offense?

Michigan fans seem split.

Analysts seem split.

Honestly, Michigan might be split.

Either way, whoever takes the first snap is going to have the pleasure of doing it in front of a loud Autzen crowd that's still riding the momentum from the Ohio State win.

Not exactly an easy assignment.

### Looking Ahead

The Pick'em race remains crowded.

Sco remains in first.

Talesofderp grabs a crucial bonus point.

The Ducks just picked up one of the biggest wins of the season.

And now Michigan heads to Eugene with a quarterback question hanging over the entire game.

Sounds like another interesting week is ahead.

As always, make your picks wisely.

History suggests you probably won't. 🦆🏈


